menu "Telegram bot service"

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_MAX_USERS
        int "Maximum number of authorized users"
        range 1 64
        default 8
        help
            Size of the static table holding the users allowed to interact
            with the bot.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_MAX_CHATS
        int "Maximum number of allowed group chats"
        range 1 32
        default 4
        help
            Size of the static table holding the group chats the bot serves.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_MAX_COMMANDS
        int "Maximum number of registered commands"
        range 16 64
        default 20
        help
            Size of the static command table. The fourteen built-in
            commands are registered in this same table, so anything below
            fifteen leaves no room for a command of your own and anything
            below fourteen makes telegram_init() fail outright. The lower
            bound of this range is set accordingly; the default leaves six
            free slots.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_MAX_CALLBACKS
        int "Maximum number of inline button handlers"
        range 1 32
        default 4
        help
            Size of the static table routing inline button payloads to
            handlers by prefix. The built-in /menu command registers its
            own, so leave room for it; raise this to match the number of
            button prefixes the application adds on top.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_MAX_PARAMS
        int "Maximum number of remotely configurable parameters"
        range 1 32
        default 4
        help
            Size of the static table holding the parameters exposed through
            the /config, /get and /set commands. Raise it to match the
            number of parameters the application actually registers.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_MAX_SENSORS
        int "Maximum number of published sensors"
        range 1 32
        default 4
        help
            Size of the static table holding the sensors exposed through the
            /sensors and /status commands. Raise it to match the number of
            sensors the application actually publishes.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_RX_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Default size of the update reception buffer"
        range 1024 32768
        default 2048
        help
            Default capacity of the buffer holding one getUpdates answer.
            An answer larger than this is skipped and reported, so the
            default trades a rare long batch for heap that a TLS handshake
            needs in one contiguous piece. Increase it when updates carry
            long texts, when several updates are delivered in a single
            batch, or on a board with memory to spare.

    config TELEGRAM_SERVICE_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Default stack size of the service task"
        range 4096 32768
        default 8192
        help
            Default stack size in bytes of the task created by
            telegram_start(). TLS and JSON parsing dominate this figure.

endmenu
